__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.egg-info/
# Anchored. `build/` unanchored also matches `transformation/build/` — the Construction Compiler —
# so a new module added there was ignored in silence while its neighbours stayed tracked, which is
# the worst form of the failure: the package half-exists in the repo.
/build/
/dist/
.venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
CLAUDE.md

# Build output. A compiled projection is DERIVED from source by the compiler and regenerated by
# every build: tracking it dirties the repo on each rebuild, fails the release preflight, and ships
# a derivation as if it were source. Declared from the first commit — snapshot_inspector learned
# this the hard way, having tracked 47 compiled files until release 3.
compiled/
**/compiled/
snapshot/

# Dossiers are evidence ABOUT a composition, not part of one. Generated dossiers stay local;
# authored ones are tracked, and they share this directory.
#
# No allowlist of named directories: an allowlist is a hand-kept copy, and a delivered dossier
# stays untracked and unbacked for as long as nobody remembers to add its name.
#
# The two kinds differ in shape, so the shape is what decides. An authored dossier is
# `dossiers/<subject>/` and holds documents; a generated one is `dossiers/<domain>/<subdomain>/` and
# holds a directory. Ignoring the nested level ignores everything generated and nothing authored,
# and a new authored dossier is tracked from the moment it exists.
/dossiers/*/*/

# Construction determination records — evidence about a build, not build output.
# `3e` §3.2 makes evidence output only; nothing reads these.
snapshot/determinations/
**/snapshot/determinations/
# Packaging output at the root — not the `transformation/build` package.
/build/
dist/
*.py[cod]
